## With real data



[credentialform_lnirt](https://itemresponsewarehouse.org/tables/credentialform_lnirt/) is the main example: a long, high-stakes test. [roar_lexical](https://itemresponsewarehouse.org/tables/roar_lexical/) is the contrast: a task answered in under a second, reused from [Guessing and priors](guessing-priors.qmd) for its rapid responses. [rapm_poulton_2022_timed](https://itemresponsewarehouse.org/tables/rapm_poulton_2022_timed/) and [rapm_poulton_2022_untimed](https://itemresponsewarehouse.org/tables/rapm_poulton_2022_untimed/) do one job together: the same 12 items with and without a clock, the nearest these tables come to forcing speed. [Download the code](code/response-time-irw.R); it needs `lme4`.

### A licensure exam

One form of a credentialing exam, a dataset with suspected cheating from the [*Handbook of quantitative methods for detecting cheating on tests*](https://doi.org/10.4324/9781315743097) (Cizek & Wollack, 2016) and distributed with [`LNIRT`](https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/LNIRT/index.html). Keying: 1 is a correct answer.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="show"}
library(lme4)
options(digits = 7)  # R's default, in case a .Rprofile changes it
url <- "https://redivis.com/api/v1/tables/datapages.item_response_warehouse:v60_0.credentialform_lnirt/rows?format=csv"
cf <- read.csv(url)
# One row per response; resp is 1 for a correct answer, rt the time on the item in
# whole seconds. Items iraw.1-170 are the scored items, which everyone answered.
# iraw.171-200 hold pilot items, and which pilot items sit under a name depends on
# the respondent's pilot set (Pretest), so we keep the scored items only.
cf$inum <- as.integer(sub("iraw.", "", cf$item))
cf <- cf[cf$inum <= 170, ]
c(respondents = length(unique(cf$id)), items = length(unique(cf$item)),
  missing = sum(is.na(cf$resp)), time_zero = sum(cf$rt == 0))
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
respondents       items     missing   time_zero 
       1636         170           0         105 
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="show"}
# A time of 0 means under a second; log(0) is undefined, so those rows are set aside.
cf <- cf[cf$rt > 0, ]
cf$lrt <- log(cf$rt)
round(c(accuracy = mean(cf$resp), median_s = median(cf$rt), mean_s = mean(cf$rt),
        max_s = max(cf$rt)), 2)
```

