Abler respondents are faster ($r = 0.30$), and harder items take longer ($r = 0.48$): rough versions of $\rho$ and its item-level counterpart.

::: {.callout-tip appearance="simple"}
**Recall** from [Classical test theory and reliability](ctt-reliability.qmd) (problem 2): an observed correlation is the correlation of true scores times the square root of the two reliabilities ([Spearman, 1904](https://doi.org/10.2307/1412159)). Estimated abilities and speeds have errors too, so their correlation understates $\rho$, most with few items; a joint fit estimates $\rho$ directly.
:::

